Structurally sound: three panes on a uniform 4px gutter (borders at x=4/686/691/1144/1149/1435), 9px content insets in all four panes, numeric columns sharing a right edge at x=1134, identity bar optically centred (ink y18-44 in a 0-63 band) and not wrapping at 1440.

Iteration changes. (1) Landed: the provenance sentences set flush-left at x=1158, the same edge as every row label; the DATA row now spans y208-450 = 29% of the pane's 827px visible height (prose alone 24.7%), down from 39-41%. It brought finding 2. (2) Not verifiable: no `COST · TRANSACTIONFEE` row is on screen — the pane clips first (finding 1). No zero-padded hex word appears in any visible row. (3) Not on this surface. (4) Landed: `⊘` on line 29, `⊙` on line 32, both centred at x≈78 with the `·` marks, no shift to the code's left edge (x=130 throughout). (5) Landed: the exit reads `← demo`.

Call Trace emptiness, measured here: the tabbed region is y68-561 = 494px; the last content pixel is y=320; 241px, 48.9%, is empty. Against the frame list below the column header (y126-561) it is 53.1%. The 47-57% observation holds; 76-91% does not reproduce at laptop. But half the premise fails: Values does not overflow — content ends y=851 in a pane ending y=895, 87% full. The pane that overflows is Transaction, in the other column, which this weight cannot feed.

